From: Cinders of Chaos <noreply@cindersofchaos.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:07:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Render: skip selection lookups while nothing is selected

renderCollectChunkInstances() ran up to three QHash lookups per quad
(entity twice, selected once) to compute the selection flag. Chunks are
collected again after every edit and after every item animation phase,
so with water and other animated items on screen this ran for every quad
of every visible chunk several times per second. With an empty selection
the flag is always 0; the lookups are now skipped in that case. The
result is identical.
---
 editor/map/mapview_render.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/editor/map/mapview_render.cpp b/editor/map/mapview_render.cpp
index 14e3183..2962b4d 100644
--- a/editor/map/mapview_render.cpp
+++ b/editor/map/mapview_render.cpp
@@ -88,11 +88,14 @@ quint32 MapView::renderCollectChunkInstances(int z, quint64 key, bool groundOnly
     }
 
     out.reserve(quads->size() * 6);
+    // With an empty selection every quad is unselected; skip the three hash
+    // lookups per quad (chunks are collected again on each animation phase).
+    const bool anySelected = !m_selectionController.selected().isEmpty();
     for (const QuadRef &q : *quads) {
         if (groundOnly && !q.ground) continue;
         const QRect &slot = atlasSlots[static_cast<size_t>(q.atlasSlot)];
 
-        const float sel = ((m_selectionController.wholeStack()
+        const float sel = (anySelected && (m_selectionController.wholeStack()
                            || (m_selectionController.entity(selKey(q.tileX, q.tileY, z)) != -1
                                ? q.itemIndex == m_selectionController.entity(selKey(q.tileX, q.tileY, z))
                                : q.topItem))
